# Gradle: generally available versions

Pin the **latest generally available** release of the line already in use (Kotlin bugfix, Gradle patch, platform micro). Do not take the next feature, preview, milestone, snapshot, RC, alpha, or beta.

If **no GA** exists that can compile this language, JDK, and Gradle, keep the current compatible pre-release. Do not downgrade to an older GA that cannot build. Do not jump to a newer pre-release just because it exists.

Keep one version for a family: Kotlin `jvm` and `allopen` match; Quarkus plugin, platform BOM, and Google Cloud services BOM match. Direct libraries not on a BOM use the latest **stable** Maven Central coordinate.

Do not declare `kotlin-stdlib-jdk7` or `kotlin-stdlib-jdk8`. Those artefacts merged into `kotlin-stdlib`; the Kotlin Gradle plugin already adds it.

Upgrade the wrapper with the same distribution type (`bin` or `all`). Set `distributionSha256Sum` from the official checksum for that zip.

```properties
# gradle.properties — plugin and BOM are the same GA micro
quarkusPluginId=io.quarkus
quarkusPluginVersion=3.38.2
quarkusPlatformGroupId=io.quarkus.platform
quarkusPlatformArtifactId=quarkus-bom
quarkusPlatformVersion=3.38.2
```

```properties
# gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties — latest GA patch of this Gradle line
distributionBase=GRADLE_USER_HOME
distributionPath=wrapper/dists
distributionSha256Sum=61ba77b3ff7167e60962763eb4bae79db7120c189b9544358d0ade3c1e712a83
distributionUrl=https\://services.gradle.org/distributions/gradle-9.6.1-all.zip
validateDistributionUrl=true
```

```kotlin
plugins {
    kotlin("jvm") version "2.4.10"
    kotlin("plugin.allopen") version "2.4.10"
}

dependencies {
    implementation(enforcedPlatform("$quarkusPlatformGroupId:$quarkusPlatformArtifactId:$quarkusPlatformVersion"))
    implementation(enforcedPlatform("$quarkusPlatformGroupId:quarkus-google-cloud-services-bom:$quarkusPlatformVersion"))
    // Do not add org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib-jdk8
}
```
